{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":19307,"name":"Ishashah","username":"ishashah","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/i/f475e1/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-07-29T17:50:16.232Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi all,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe strongly recommend using direct paths to access the data in the code execution environment rather than using \u003ccode\u003eglob()\u003c/code\u003e . First import \u003ccode\u003e/code_execution/data/submission_format.csv\u003c/code\u003e , and then use the UIDs in the submission format to build paths to the nifti images: \u003ccode\u003e/code_execution/data/niftis/{uid_from_submission_format_row}.nii.gz\u003c/code\u003e . Often it takes ~15-20 seconds for the data to mount and allow listing or glob, but direct path access (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/drivendataorg/competition-sfmn-parkinsons-runtime/tree/main/examples\"\u003eas demonstrated in the examples in our runtime repo\u003c/a\u003e) should work immediately. Please let us know if you have any questions, and thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-07-29T17:50:16.232Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":10,"readers_count":9,"score":37.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":11467,"topic_slug":"accessing-data-in-code-execution-environment","display_username":"Ishashah","primary_group_name":"drivendata-staff","flair_name":"drivendata-staff","flair_url":"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex028/uploads/drivendata1/original/2X/c/ccc07e6a647e62601ee79f5014eac0f94bc81547.png","flair_bg_color":"efefef","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/drivendataorg/competition-sfmn-parkinsons-runtime/tree/main/examples","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"competition-sfmn-parkinsons-runtime/ex